# Semgrep for the scan-and-gate CI job, in its own venv: it pins its dependencies tightly, so it
# can't share a resolver with bandit/checkov (requirements-scanners.in). Edit THIS file, then
# regenerate the lock:
#   uv pip compile requirements-semgrep.in --generate-hashes --python-version 3.12 \
#     --python-platform x86_64-manylinux_2_28 --exclude-newer <today minus 14 days> \
#     --exclude-newer-package certifi=2026-10-21 -o requirements-semgrep.txt
# Then re-add the security-exception lines at the end of requirements-semgrep.txt (uv drops them;
# without them the gate reports the two as new again).
# Install with: pip install --require-hashes -r requirements-semgrep.txt
#
# Cooldown exception (--exclude-newer-package), the oldest release that fixes a finding:
#   certifi 2026.10.19   GHSA-6q48-6c7w-9gw2 (CRITICAL), released 2026-10-20
# Not upgradable: semgrep 1.179.0 pins mcp==1.29.0 and opentelemetry-api~=1.37.0; see the
# exception lines in requirements-semgrep.txt.
semgrep==1.179.0
